{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1956","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1956","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1956\",\"parent_revision\":\"0d43da8808a2328602fc88e2eb0e612d6e2b23de\",\"root_revision\":\"05543a9f139e465023ea0ff0c3b47c22deda4aa48cfa9df27460b00cb1eea40c\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: feat: Add doctest-as-tests guidance to python3-testing skill\\nDate: 2026-04-27\\nGoal: Add doctest-as-tests guidance to the python3-testing skill so developers know when and how to use doctest for pure-function example validation.\\nConditions:\\n1. python3-testing SKILL.md exists and is readable | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. Doctest guidance is absent from python3-testing | Status: AVAILABLE\\n3. python3-test-design SKILL.md exists | Status: AVAILABLE\\n4. python3-testing/references/testing-standards.md exists | Status: AVAILABLE\\n5. python-engineering code-reviewer.md exists | Status: AVAILABLE\\n6. python3-core SKILL.md Standing Defaults section exists | Status: AVAILABLE\\n7. TheAlgorithms-Python doctest patterns are available as source | Status: AVAILABLE\\n8. No existing doctest section conflicts in any target file | Status: AVAILABLE\\n9. Doctest syntax for pytest --doctest-modules is stable | Status: AVAILABLE\\n10. Scope of change is additive (no renames or deletions) | Status: AVAILABLE\\nAVAILABLE count: 10\\nDERIVABLE count: 0\\nMISSING count: 0\\nDecision: APPROVED\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Code - Producers\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-testing/SKILL.md` \u2014 primary target; must gain a new \\\"Doctest-Embedded Examples\\\" section before the References section. Currently the canonical source for pytest patterns loaded by agents and skills. | Risk: LOW | Why: pure additive content change; no existing section is modified or removed\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-core/SKILL.md` \u2014 \\\"Testing Defaults\\\" section (line 30) must gain one new bullet: \\\"Doctests for pure-function example validation \u2014 see python3-testing for the pattern\\\". Acts as the standing-defaults router loaded on every Python task. | Risk: LOW | Why: one-line addition to an existing bullet list; no bullet is removed or rephrased\\n\\n### Code - Consumers\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/agents/python-pytest-architect.md` \u2014 loads `python3-testing` as a declared skill; after the change it inherits the doctest section. No incompatibility with current content. | Risk: LOW | Why: skill content is additive; agent quality checklist does not contradict doctest guidance\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/agents/python-cli-architect.md` \u2014 loads both `python3-core` and `python3-testing`; will inherit the updated Testing Defaults bullet. | Risk: LOW | Why: additive pointer only; agent's own testing behavior block is unchanged\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/agents/code-reviewer.md` \u2014 loads `python3-testing`; inherits new doctest section. Review criteria are additive-compatible. | Risk: LOW | Why: doctest guidance expands, does not contradict, the existing review checklist\\n\\n### Code - Other References\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-testing/references/testing-standards.md` \u2014 current reference companion to `python3-testing/SKILL.md`. Contains AAA, fixture, and coverage config but zero doctest guidance. If the SKILL.md gains a doctest section, this reference file may become incomplete for agents that load it for full testing standards context. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: documentation risk \u2014 agents loading `testing-standards.md` as a comprehensive reference will find doctest absent; consistency gap between SKILL.md and its reference\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-core/references/python3-standards.md` \u2014 unified standards document (line 71\u201378 section on Testing). Contains pytest/pytest-mock, AAA, coverage, TDD \u2014 no doctest. After the item ships, this document would be out of sync with the pointer added to `python3-core/SKILL.md`. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: documentation risk \u2014 agents loading this as the authoritative standards source will not find doctest; the SKILL.md pointer will have no backing in the standards doc\\n\\n### Tests\\nNone identified. This item adds documentation content (SKILL.md files) \u2014 there are no runtime code tests to write. Skill content is validated by `uvx skilllint@latest check` (frontmatter/schema lint), not pytest. No behavioral regression risk from test gap.\\n\\n### Documentation\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-test-design/SKILL.md` \u2014 describes test strategy selection including \\\"When to Use Unit Tests\\\" and \\\"When to Use Property-Based Tests\\\" (lines 83\u2013112). Has no doctest strategy section. After the change, agents routing through `python3-test-design` receive no signal to consider doctests as a design option for pure functions. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: documentation gap \u2014 agents using this skill to design test strategy will miss doctest as a valid choice for pure-function, parser/serializer, and algorithmic scenarios\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-tdd/SKILL.md` \u2014 TDD workflow skill that loads `python3-testing` for patterns. Its Phase 2 (\\\"Write Failing Tests\\\") and Phase 4 verification commands (`pytest --cov=src`) do not mention `--doctest-modules`. Post-change, the quality gate checklist may be materially incomplete for projects where doctests are the chosen strategy for pure functions. | Risk: LOW | Why: TDD workflow is intact; doctest is an optional strategy addition, not a replacement; LOW because omission here is minor \u2014 agents will find the pattern via the loaded `python3-testing` skill\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 plugin architecture doc listing specialist skills. Does not enumerate doctest guidance anywhere. No content here would become stale from the item. | Risk: LOW | Why: CLAUDE.md describes routing architecture, not testing content details; no stale claim created\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n- `pyproject.toml` (repo root, lines 354\u2013368) \u2014 `[tool.pytest.ini_options] addopts` uses list format. The snippet being added to `python3-testing/SKILL.md` must use list-format syntax (`addopts = [\\\"--doctest-modules\\\"]`) not string format. Fact-Check Claim 5 confirmed list format is the project norm. | Risk: LOW | Why: format mismatch risk only \u2014 if the snippet shows string format it would mislead agents modifying this repo's config; verified list format is correct\\n- `plugins/development-harness/pyproject.toml` (lines 32\u201341) \u2014 same list-format addopts pattern. Neither pyproject.toml includes `--doctest-modules`. No change to either file is required by this item (guidance only); but agents following the new skill content might add it. | Risk: LOW | Why: informational risk only \u2014 no current configuration breaks; agents will act only if they choose to adopt the pattern\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/agents/python-pytest-architect.md` \u2014 quality checklist (lines 34\u201344) has no doctest entry. After the change, agents running `python-pytest-architect` will have doctest guidance available via the loaded skill, but the agent's own mandatory checklist will not prompt them to consider or verify doctest setup. | Risk: LOW | Why: the agent loads the skill dynamically; the gap is a missed prompt opportunity, not an incorrect instruction \u2014 LOW because no active instruction becomes wrong\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-testing/SKILL.md` | Role: producer | Connection: primary target for new section | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-core/SKILL.md` | Role: producer | Connection: Testing Defaults section receives one-line pointer | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-testing/references/testing-standards.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: companion reference to python3-testing/SKILL.md; no doctest section after change | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-core/references/python3-standards.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: unified standards doc consulted by agents for testing defaults; will lag the SKILL.md pointer | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-test-design/SKILL.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: strategy selection skill; pure-function / parser / algorithmic scenario overlap with doctest use cases | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-tdd/SKILL.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: loads python3-testing; quality gate commands do not mention --doctest-modules | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/agents/python-pytest-architect.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: loads python3-testing; quality checklist has no doctest entry | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/agents/python-cli-architect.md` | Role: consumer | Connection: loads python3-core and python3-testing | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/agents/code-reviewer.md` | Role: consumer | Connection: loads python3-testing; review criteria additive-compatible | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `pyproject.toml` (repo root) | Role: configuration | Connection: list-format addopts snippet must match project norm | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/python-engineering/CLAUDE.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: plugin architecture doc; no stale content created | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n\\n### Risk Summary\\n- Overall system risk: LOW\\n- Highest-risk systems:\\n  - `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-testing/references/testing-standards.md` \u2014 companion reference stays incomplete; agents loading it as the authoritative standards source will not find doctest guidance after it is added to SKILL.md\\n  - `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-core/references/python3-standards.md` \u2014 unified standards doc will be out of sync with the Testing Defaults pointer added to SKILL.md; documentation drift between SKILL.md and its backing reference\\n  - `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-test-design/SKILL.md` \u2014 strategy selection skill omits doctest as a valid strategy option for pure-function / algorithmic scenarios that perfectly match the doctest use case description\\n- Main risk themes:\\n  - documentation: three reference/strategy files stay out of sync with the new guidance unless updated alongside the primary targets\\n- Scope expansion:\\n  - `python3-test-design/SKILL.md` was not in the original item description but is directly affected \u2014 it covers the same use-case scenarios (pure functions, parsers, algorithms) that doctest targets. Scope should expand to include it as an optional update target.\\n  - `python3-testing/references/testing-standards.md` and `python3-core/references/python3-standards.md` were not named in the item but are companion references that will diverge from their parent SKILL.md files without a corresponding update.\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n- [x] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [x] Every code consumer migrated or verified compatible\\n- [x] Every affected test updated or new coverage added (N/A \u2014 documentation-only change)\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated \u2014 `testing-standards.md`, `python3-standards.md`, and optionally `python3-test-design/SKILL.md` need doctest entries to stay in sync\\n- [x] Every affected config or CI path updated and validated (addopts format verified as list-style)\\n- [x] Every affected agent or skill instruction updated (agent checklists verified compatible)\\n- [x] Replacement or migration coverage gaps resolved (N/A \u2014 no migration)\\n- [x] Hidden transitive dependencies checked (specialist-skill-routing, python3-tdd verified; no blocking transitive risk found)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add doctest-as-tests guidance to python3-testing skill (pytest --doctest-modules pattern)** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/learning-resources/TheAlgorithms-Python.md \u2014 pattern: Comprehensive test coverage using doctests\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-26\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n\\n<!-- artifact-gist:1aa1b817f8bf01b3b402cc25b14be82a -->\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-27)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. Open `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-testing/SKILL.md` and search for \\\"doctest\\\" \u2014 zero matches.\\n2. Open `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-core/SKILL.md` and search for \\\"doctest\\\" \u2014 zero matches.\\n3. Open `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-test-design/SKILL.md` and search for \\\"doctest\\\" \u2014 zero matches.\\n4. Write a pure function with a `>>> ` docstring example in any Python file in the repo.\\n5. Run `pytest` without `--doctest-modules` \u2014 the docstring example is never executed, no failure reported even if the example is wrong.\\n6. Consult any python-engineering skill for guidance on docstring example validation \u2014 no guidance exists.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n6/10 \u2014 P2 (could-have).\\n\\nDocstring example drift is a latent correctness risk: examples in documentation silently diverge from actual function behavior, misleading both humans and agents. The fix is low-risk and bounded (additive content to existing skill files). However, no user-facing feature is blocked and no CI failure exists today. Priority reflects the value of closing the gap against the low urgency of undetected drift in a documentation-only context.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Any agent or developer relying on python-engineering skills to write tested documentation examples \u2014 currently receives no guidance and may omit doctest entirely.\\n- Bottleneck: `python3-testing/SKILL.md` is the authoritative source for pytest patterns in this plugin. Absence of doctest guidance means agents writing new pure functions or parsers will not add `>>> ` examples, and existing examples will not be validated.\\n- Affected files: `python3-testing/SKILL.md`, `python3-core/SKILL.md`, `python3-test-design/SKILL.md`, `python3-testing/references/testing-standards.md`, `python3-core/references/python3-standards.md`.\\n- Downstream consumers: All agents and developers using python-engineering skills to author or review Python code with docstring examples.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Docstring examples in python-engineering\u2013guided code become executable and are validated on every `pytest` run, eliminating silent example drift.\\n- Agents authoring pure functions receive a concrete pattern (when-to-use criteria + `>>> ` block format) rather than inferring from general pytest docs.\\n- Dual benefit is self-documenting: a single source produces both human-readable API examples and a test assertion \u2014 no extra test file required for simple cases.\\n- `python3-core/SKILL.md` gains a cross-reference pointer, closing the gap for agents that load only the core skill without loading the full testing skill.\\n- Companion reference files (`testing-standards.md`, `python3-standards.md`) stay consistent with the primary skill content.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen the guidance is in place:\\n\\n- `python3-testing/SKILL.md` contains a named section (e.g. \\\"Doctest-Embedded Examples\\\") that is searchable by grep for \\\"doctest\\\".\\n- The section states when doctest is appropriate (pure functions, single-result examples, parser/serializer round-trips, algorithmic functions).\\n- The section shows the pytest invocation (`pytest --doctest-modules`) and the `addopts` configuration in list format matching the repo standard.\\n- The section includes a concrete `>>> ` docstring example block that an agent can copy as a template.\\n- `python3-core/SKILL.md` Testing Defaults (around line 30) contains a one-liner cross-reference to the doctest pattern, visible via grep for \\\"doctest\\\".\\n- `python3-test-design/SKILL.md` contains a reference or equivalent note covering doctest use-case scenarios.\\n- `testing-standards.md` and `python3-standards.md` companion references are consistent with the primary skill content \u2014 each contains at least one mention of \\\"doctest\\\".\\n- Running `pytest --doctest-modules` against a file with a `>>> ` example in a docstring executes and validates the example.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `grep -n \\\"doctest\\\" plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-testing/SKILL.md` returns at least one match \u2014 section heading and body are present.\\n2. `grep -n \\\"doctest-modules\\\" plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-testing/SKILL.md` returns a match \u2014 the pytest invocation flag is documented.\\n3. `grep -n \\\"doctest\\\" plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-core/SKILL.md` returns at least one match \u2014 the cross-reference one-liner is present.\\n4. `grep -n \\\"doctest\\\" plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-test-design/SKILL.md` returns at least one match \u2014 use-case coverage is present.\\n5. `grep -n \\\"doctest\\\" plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-testing/references/testing-standards.md` returns at least one match.\\n6. `grep -n \\\"doctest\\\" plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-core/references/python3-standards.md` returns at least one match.\\n7. `grep -n \\\"addopts\\\" plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-testing/SKILL.md` returns a match where the value uses list format (`addopts = [...]`), not string format (`addopts = \\\"...\\\"`).\\n8. `grep -n '>>>' plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-testing/SKILL.md` returns at least one match \u2014 a concrete docstring example block is present.\\n9. The `python3-testing/SKILL.md` section passes `uv run prek run --files plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-testing/SKILL.md` with no lint errors.\\n10. The `python3-core/SKILL.md` file passes `uv run prek run --files plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-core/SKILL.md` with no lint errors.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Source pattern | `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-testing/references/TheAlgorithms-Python.md` lines 104, 175, 178, 181, 221, 227 \u2014 validated `pytest --doctest-modules` pattern |\\n| Primary target | `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-testing/SKILL.md` |\\n| Cross-reference target | `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-core/SKILL.md` |\\n| Scope-expanded target | `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-test-design/SKILL.md` |\\n| Companion reference | `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-testing/references/testing-standards.md` |\\n| Companion reference | `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-core/references/python3-standards.md` |\\n| Repo standard evidence | Root `pyproject.toml` and plugin `pyproject.toml` \u2014 both confirmed using list format `addopts = [...]` |\\n| Skill | /python-engineering:python3-testing |\\n| Skill | /python-engineering:python3-core |\\n| Skill | /python-engineering:python3-test-design |\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n| File | Change | Risk |\\n|------|--------|------|\\n| `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-testing/SKILL.md` | New \\\"Doctest-Embedded Examples\\\" section before References | LOW \u2014 additive only |\\n| `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-core/SKILL.md` | One-liner cross-reference added to Testing Defaults (~line 30) | LOW \u2014 additive, single line |\\n| `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-test-design/SKILL.md` | Doctest use-case scenario note added | MEDIUM \u2014 requires locating correct insertion point in existing structure |\\n| `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-testing/references/testing-standards.md` | Companion reference updated to include doctest pattern | MEDIUM \u2014 must stay consistent with SKILL.md content |\\n| `plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-core/references/python3-standards.md` | Testing section (lines 70\u201378) updated with doctest reference | MEDIUM \u2014 requires care to preserve existing section formatting |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 all source material and target files are present in the repo. RT-ICA assessed READY (10/10 AVAILABLE).\\n- Blocks: None identified in the current backlog. No downstream items are waiting on this guidance being present.\\n- Sequencing note: Changes to `python3-core/SKILL.md` and the companion reference files should be made after the primary `python3-testing/SKILL.md` section is finalized, so cross-references point to stable content.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 The work is entirely additive: new prose sections and cross-reference lines in existing skill markdown files. No code changes, no schema changes, no test infrastructure modifications. Five files are touched; the largest change (the primary SKILL.md section) is a single bounded section insert. Companion reference updates are one-liners or short paragraphs. Linting after each file is the main validation step.\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n**Alignment assessment**: NOT_APPLICABLE\\n**Rationale**: This is an additive documentation change \u2014 no prior implementation of doctest guidance exists in python3-testing to diverge from. There is no existing design intent to compare against; the feature-context artifact confirms this is net-new guidance. Alignment analysis is not applicable to additive-only changes with no prior interface.\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: unbounded-design\\n\\n**Rationale**: The item describes a missing documentation section about doctest patterns in python-engineering testing skills. This is not a surface fix (Q1 fails), not a recurring failure pattern (Q2 \u2014 only one comparable prior item), not a reproducible defect (Q3 \u2014 no failure to trace), and not a missing validation gate (Q4 \u2014 no gate should have prevented this). The fix requires design framing: choosing what content to create, how to structure the doctest section, which examples best illustrate the pattern, and how deeply to integrate the guidance across the four target files.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: N/A \u2014 unbounded-design does not require root-cause analysis\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: Docstring examples drift silently from implementation because no test executes them \u2192 Doctest section integrated into python3-testing/SKILL.md with pytest configuration and examples, allowing agents to discover and validate docstring examples as tested code\\n\\n## Source Pattern\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nFrom TheAlgorithms-Python.md, \\\"Code Quality Standards\\\" and \\\"Test Execution\\\":\\n> \\\"Each algorithm includes doctests in the docstring that validate: Normal cases, Edge cases, Type diversity, Correctness verification (against Python's built-in `sorted()`)\\\"\\n> `pytest --doctest-modules --showlocals`\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRun: `grep -rn \\\"doctest\\\" plugins/python-engineering/skills/python3-testing/SKILL.md` returns at least one section heading referencing doctests. The `pyproject.toml` snippet contains the literal stri